Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:49:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Offer the setup AI the outfits the Studio dresses from,
 keyed by id

Real AI runs (Gemini 3 Flash via OpenRouter, 10 Nov) showed two problems
with the labelled outfit list:
- The model once copied a whole "id: name (labels)" line as the outfit id,
  so the pick was dropped (logged) and the character started in the white
  T-shirt. Outfits are now an object keyed by id.
- The list came from each avatar's own outfit ids (120 women's ids, 45 of
  them race-baked copies or old custom ids the Studio never shows). It now
  comes from the avatar set list the Studio dresses a character from (75
  women's, 64 men's), else the avatar's own list.

The set rule now asks only for sets from the brief's own world or period
that show the same kind of place, and an empty list when none fits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
